Credits - work this project builds on or learned from (ideas and formats, no code unless listed above):

* ggml / llama.cpp (Georgi Gerganov and contributors): the GGUF file format and the K-quant and IQ block layouts that
  TQLLM reads natively, and the reference engine every result is compared against.
* Qwen team, Alibaba: the Qwen3.5 / Qwen3.8 models and the Qwen3-VL vision encoder design.
* z-lab: DFlash2, the block-diffusion draft model used for speculative decoding.
* spiritbuun (buun-llama-cpp): the trellis-coded quantisation idea behind the tcq KV-cache codecs (own codebooks and code).
* Google Research: TurboQuant (ICLR 2026), the rotation-plus-codebook lineage the TQ3 / TQ4 formats follow.
* TheTom (turboquant_plus): TurboQuant KV-cache ideas and the REFRACT distance-from-reference quality metric.
* Avarok (TorQuant): learned rotations for quantisation.
* Unsloth: the UD GGUF quantisations, which TQLLM runs natively and benchmarks against.
* Strata (MIT, Niko1221 and the Strata contributors): the idea of launching MMQ directly per expert group from the
  prefill path.
* Splash (Apache-2.0): the staged prefill GEMM tile on Apple GPUs (weights dequantized once per threadgroup into a
  double-buffered threadgroup stage, one matmul2d per simdgroup per step), reimplemented for the NAX 4-bit layout.

The full credits table, including methods and comparison baselines, is in README.md (Credits).
